# SOURCE: etc/release.manifest
# STARDATE: 2026-07-30
# STATUS: data, not code — WHAT ships from bin/ into $PREFIX/bin, one entry per line.
#
# Consumed by etc/deploy-release.sh (copy + chmod + PATH symlinks) and by the provisioning doctor
# (deploy/modules.d/60-deploy.sh check). The installer and the doctor are BLIND
# to content: add or remove a shipped file HERE, never in code. Before this file the list
# existed twice (install.sh code + etc/README.md procedure) and the copies had started to drift.
#
# Format: <bin-file> <exec|noexec> [link]
#   exec / noexec  whether the installed file carries +x. The MCP bridge is noexec on purpose:
#                  it is invoked as `python3 <path>` (config/runtime.exs mcp_server_spec) and
#                  only needs group-read.
#   link           the entry also gets a PATH symlink $LINK_DIR/<name> -> $PREFIX/bin/<name>
#                  (pointer symlinks ONLY — copies are the dead D3 invention).
#
# bin/claude_launch.identity SHIPS: the runtime runs bin/publish-transform.sh host-side (the
# `project_publish` worker; `lcars publish run` is the human door to the same rail), and that
# script sources the co-located identity for co-author attribution — the runtime invocation makes
# it a dependency (cf. etc/README.md). Same reason for the publish scripts: they live in bin/ so
# the manifest can carry them.
fleet                   exec   link
lcars                      exec   link
bwrap_launch.sh            exec
host_launch.sh             exec
claude_launch.sh           exec
publish-transform.sh       exec
publish-rail.sh            exec
# Les deux moities Python de publish-transform, noexec pour la meme raison que le pont MCP : l'une
# est lancee `python3 <path>`, l'autre est LUE par git-filter-repo (`--commit-callback FILE`).
# Absentes de $PREFIX/bin, le script echoue a la borne ou a la reecriture — elles s'installent avec
# lui ou pas du tout.
publish-transform-boundary.py     noexec
publish-transform-attribution.py  noexec
forge-cli.sh               exec
claude_launch.identity     noexec
# La declaration d'endpoints du vendor, LUE A COTE de son launcher (Egress.Vendor derive le chemin
# depuis celui du launcher). Absente de $PREFIX/bin, le proxy d'egress sert une allowlist VIDE et
# le pod ne joint meme pas son modele — constate au banc : le mur refusait api.anthropic.com.
# Un launcher de vendor et sa declaration s'installent ensemble ou pas du tout.
claude_launch.egress       noexec
fleet_mcp_stdio_bridge.py  noexec
